{"id": "police-overtime-limits-not-enforced", "title": "Police overtime: nine limits exceeded, cards self-approved, one investigation", "seconds": 161.7, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "f109f9f087adfec7", "words": 427, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]", "oneLine"], "text": "Nine overtime limits. The Police Department broke every one of them, year after year.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.17, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "9", "label": "overtime limits tested", "sub": "Police Department, fiscal 2018-19 to 2022-23"}, "emph": ["every one"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.87, 1.75, 1.91, 2.19, 2.59, 2.92, 3.31, 3.5, 3.59, 3.81, 4.26, 4.62]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["amount", "timeline[4]"], "text": "So what did police overtime cost in fiscal 2023?", "t0": 5.29, "t1": 8.59, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Police overtime", "sub": "fiscal 2022-23, all funds"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.32, 0.47, 0.8, 1.27, 1.7, 1.82, 2.18, 2.44]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "timeline[4]"], "text": "108,373,261 dollars, in the City’s own financial system.", "t0": 8.59, "t1": 12.84, "shot": "b1a", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$108,373,261", "label": "police overtime, fiscal 2022-23, all funds", "sub": "the audit’s figure from the City’s financial system"}, "emph": ["108,373,261"], "wt": [0.04, 0.32, 0.53, 0.87, 1.07, 1.32, 1.6, 1.96, 2.65, 2.78, 2.88, 3.2, 3.4, 3.86]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["status", "timeline[5]", "actors[0]", "links[0]"], "text": "That’s an official finding, from the Board’s Budget and Legislative Analyst, in December 2024.", "t0": 13.36, "t1": 20.35, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "kicker": "An official finding", "sub": "Performance Audit of Police Department Overtime, 12 December 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.8, 0.97, 1.4, 2.44, 2.62, 2.74, 3.14, 3.43, 3.55, 4.07, 5.14, 5.32, 5.98, 6.3]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["status", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "It does not find that overtime was paid for hours not worked.", "t0": 20.47, "t1": 23.38, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "kicker": "An official finding", "sub": "Performance Audit of Police Department Overtime, 12 December 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.26, 0.44, 0.72, 0.86, 1.35, 1.5, 1.75, 1.92, 2.34, 2.55]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "The first finding.", "t0": 23.6, "t1": 24.58, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "kicker": "The first finding", "label": "Nine limits", "sub": "overtime hours a year, a pay period, a week and a day"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.51]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "Caps apply to overtime hours a year, a pay period, a week and a day.", "t0": 24.7, "t1": 29.17, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "kicker": "The first finding", "label": "Nine limits", "sub": "overtime hours a year, a pay period, a week and a day"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.73, 0.87, 1.44, 1.82, 1.93, 2.61, 2.74, 2.98, 3.61, 3.76, 3.96, 4.06, 4.13]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "In fiscal 2022-23,", "t0": 29.29, "t1": 32.24, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Limits broken, fiscal 2022-23", "sub": "limits in force all year", "rows": [["Over 40 overtime hours in a pay period", "7,391"], ["Over 20 overtime hours in a week", "16,688"], ["Over 72 hours worked in a week", "8,240"], ["Over 16 hours in a day", "6,057"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.61, 0.93, 1.65, 1.82]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "more than 40 overtime hours in a pay period: 7,391 times.", "t0": 32.24, "t1": 37.57, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Limits broken, fiscal 2022-23", "sub": "limits in force all year", "rows": [["Over 40 overtime hours in a pay period", "7,391"], ["Over 20 overtime hours in a week", "16,688"], ["Over 72 hours worked in a week", "8,240"], ["Over 16 hours in a day", "6,057"]]}, "emph": ["7,391"], "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.4, 0.77, 1.17, 1.47, 1.56, 1.62, 1.84, 2.75, 3.12, 3.54, 3.78, 4.09, 4.78]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "share", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[1]", "links[6]"], "text": "And 209 people, 12 percent of those working overtime, worked 32 percent of the hours.", "t0": 37.69, "t1": 43.67, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 32, "label": "of overtime hours, worked by 209 people: 12% of sworn staff who worked overtime"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.35, 0.69, 1.01, 1.42, 1.89, 2.19, 2.26, 2.49, 2.81, 3.87, 4.24, 4.83, 5.28, 5.4, 5.52]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "The second finding: the checks. Unscheduled overtime is approved verbally, and the signed card is the record.", "t0": 43.89, "t1": 50.73, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "kicker": "The second finding", "label": "The overtime card", "sub": "unscheduled overtime is approved verbally"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.57, 1.33, 1.49, 2.55, 3.16, 3.65, 3.8, 4.29, 5.25, 5.39, 5.5, 5.86, 6.22, 6.36, 6.47]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]", "links[1]", "actors[3]"], "text": "Of 559 cards sampled, 18 showed a lieutenant or sergeant approving their own overtime.", "t0": 50.85, "t1": 56.73, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "559 overtime cards sampled", "sub": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, December 2024", "rows": [["Missing a required signature", "48"], ["Same signature twice", "8"], ["A lieutenant or sergeant approving their own overtime", "18"]]}, "emph": ["their own overtime"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.53, 0.85, 1.37, 1.75, 2.54, 3.14, 3.39, 3.46, 3.88, 4.03, 4.47, 4.99, 5.16, 5.33]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]", "established[6]"], "text": "One investigation of excessive overtime in five years.", "t0": 56.85, "t1": 59.62, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["One", "investigation"], "sub": "of excessive overtime, in five years · civilian complaints, 2024-2026: none of 7,350 about overtime"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.81, 0.91, 1.37, 1.89, 2.01, 2.31]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "innocent[2]", "actors[5]"], "text": "The third finding. 10B overtime is work that outside bodies pay for.", "t0": 60.14, "t1": 64.3, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "kicker": "The third finding", "label": "10B overtime", "sub": "work outside bodies pay for; outside the overtime cap"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.45, 1.5, 1.88, 2.4, 2.54, 2.75, 2.89, 3.36, 3.69, 3.88]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "The officers’ agreement bars heavy sick-leave users from it.", "t0": 64.42, "t1": 67.2, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "kicker": "The third finding", "label": "10B overtime", "sub": "work outside bodies pay for; outside the overtime cap"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.57, 0.96, 1.42, 1.69, 2.14, 2.45, 2.62]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]", "links[2]"], "text": "Yet the audit counts 51,206 ineligible hours,", "t0": 67.32, "t1": 71.79, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "51,206", "label": "ineligible 10B overtime hours", "sub": "January 2021 to June 2023"}, "emph": ["51,206"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.35, 0.68, 1.03, 1.54, 1.98, 2.26, 2.6, 3.03, 3.74]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]", "links[2]"], "text": "from 2021 to 2023.", "t0": 71.79, "t1": 73.98, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "51,206", "label": "ineligible 10B overtime hours", "sub": "January 2021 to June 2023"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.48, 1.2, 1.36, 1.61]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]", "timeline[1]", "links[3]"], "text": "A 2021 review found more than 400 ineligible. The rule was not enforced.", "t0": 74.1, "t1": 79.65, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "a1", "kicker": "Performance Audit, December 2024", "text": "The review found more than 400 employees ineligible to work 10B assignments; the provision was not enforced", "mark": "not enforced"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.41, 0.87, 1.36, 1.65, 1.82, 2.02, 2.43, 2.88, 4.12, 4.31, 4.63, 4.8, 4.98]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "The fourth finding: General Fund overtime ran 54.8 million dollars over its original budget.", "t0": 79.87, "t1": 86.33, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$54.8 million", "label": "General Fund overtime above its original budget", "sub": "fiscal 2022-23"}, "emph": ["54.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 1.47, 1.93, 2.23, 2.75, 3.02, 3.64, 3.95, 4.22, 4.55, 5.27, 5.54, 5.67, 6.07]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "The Controller’s budget file shows overtime over budget every year from 2019 to 2026.", "t0": 86.45, "t1": 92.2, "shot": "b13a", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Over budget every year, fiscal 2019-2026", "a": ["Overtime budgeted, all funds", "$348.0 million"], "b": ["Overtime paid", "$739.0 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.68, 0.99, 1.36, 1.67, 2.23, 2.42, 2.79, 3.13, 3.69, 3.9, 4.21, 4.7, 4.82, 5.09]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "In all, it paid 2.12 times its budget, the highest ratio of 12 departments.", "t0": 92.32, "t1": 98.64, "shot": "b13a", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Over budget every year, fiscal 2019-2026", "a": ["Overtime budgeted, all funds", "$348.0 million"], "b": ["Overtime paid", "$739.0 million"]}, "emph": ["2.12 times"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.93, 1.09, 1.35, 1.64, 1.98, 2.44, 3.04, 3.4, 3.55, 4.35, 4.51, 4.85, 5.34, 5.46, 5.77]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "timeline[3]", "links[4]", "actors[6]"], "text": "In March 2023 the Department needed 25.4 million from the City’s General Reserve.", "t0": 98.76, "t1": 104.72, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "General Reserve", "sub": "a transfer to pay for overtime, March 2023", "chip": "$25.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.51, 0.81, 1.7, 1.85, 2.26, 2.58, 3.2, 3.5, 3.78, 4.43, 4.61, 4.71, 5.06, 5.42]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why", "established[3]"], "text": "Special initiatives took 319,945 overtime hours,", "t0": 104.84, "t1": 110.85, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "319,945", "label": "overtime hours on special initiatives", "sub": "an estimated $30,824,783 over five years"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.99, 1.2, 1.43, 1.74, 2.2, 3.07, 3.35, 3.74, 4.5, 5.04]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why", "established[3]"], "text": "while 911 response times rose.", "t0": 110.85, "t1": 113.5, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "319,945", "label": "overtime hours on special initiatives", "sub": "an estimated $30,824,783 over five years"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.33, 0.58, 0.85, 1.24, 1.76, 2.15]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "A complaint that an employee offered coworkers money to call in sick was closed for insufficient evidence.", "t0": 113.62, "t1": 120.53, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "closed for insufficient evidence", "kicker": "A complaint investigated in fiscal 2022-23"}, "wt": [0.0, 1.14, 1.61, 1.75, 1.83, 2.45, 2.77, 3.34, 3.59, 3.7, 3.95, 4.08, 4.78, 5.02, 5.72, 5.9, 6.45]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[5]", "timeline[7]"], "text": "The audit stops in June 2023.", "t0": 120.75, "t1": 122.76, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Police overtime, payroll, fiscal 2019", "$62.8 million"], "b": ["Police overtime, payroll, fiscal 2026", "$163.4 million"], "kicker": "Since the audit"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.46, 0.81, 0.94, 1.18, 1.44]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[5]", "timeline[7]"], "text": "Payroll police overtime reached 163.4 million dollars in fiscal 2026.", "t0": 122.88, "t1": 129.23, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Police overtime, payroll, fiscal 2019", "$62.8 million"], "b": ["Police overtime, payroll, fiscal 2026", "$163.4 million"], "kicker": "Since the audit"}, "emph": ["163.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.78, 1.38, 1.74, 1.94, 2.38, 3.31, 3.6, 3.83, 4.13, 4.81, 5.0, 5.36, 5.64]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "timeline[6]", "notEstablished[4]", "actors[1]"], "text": "The Department told the Board about 85 percent is done or well under way, without saying which.", "t0": 129.35, "t1": 135.17, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "approximately 85% of the agreed-upon recommendations", "kicker": "Police Department to the Board, 30 April 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.55, 0.83, 0.95, 1.29, 1.62, 2.32, 2.71, 2.9, 3.23, 3.44, 3.72, 3.94, 4.79, 5.16, 5.45]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Not on file: whether the limits have held since June 2023, or the 10B bills were paid.", "t0": 135.39, "t1": 141.1, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Whether the limits have been kept since June 2023", "Whether the 10B hours were billed and paid in full", "Whether the 2026 bargaining changed the sick-leave test"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.44, 1.23, 1.5, 1.61, 1.9, 2.03, 2.31, 2.58, 2.86, 3.09, 4.15, 4.3, 4.41, 4.84, 5.15, 5.3]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "innocent[1]", "innocent[3]", "actors[7]"], "text": "Full-duty staffing fell 21 percent, to 1,474,", "t0": 141.22, "t1": 146.1, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Full-duty sworn staff, January 2019", "1,868"], "b": ["Full-duty sworn staff, September 2023", "1,474"], "kicker": "Staffing fell 21%"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.47, 0.88, 1.16, 1.61, 2.32, 2.52, 3.41, 3.8]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "innocent[1]", "innocent[3]", "actors[7]"], "text": "and the limits have exceptions for emergencies.", "t0": 146.1, "t1": 148.35, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Full-duty sworn staff, January 2019", "1,868"], "b": ["Full-duty sworn staff, September 2023", "1,474"], "kicker": "Staffing fell 21%"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.33, 0.67, 0.83, 1.39, 1.55]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The Department’s overtime records since the audit, and the 10B billing ledger.", "t0": 148.47, "t1": 153.54, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The Department’s overtime and leave records for fiscal 2024 to 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "The 10B billing and collection ledger"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.32, 0.6, 1.29, 1.44, 1.88, 2.3, 2.65, 2.87, 2.99, 3.63, 3.79, 3.91, 4.45, 4.75]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "The Department agreed in full or in part with 26 of 29 recommendations.", "t0": 153.66, "t1": 158.42, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.52, 0.99, 1.16, 1.57, 1.76, 1.9, 2.41, 2.64, 3.37, 3.46, 3.93]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 158.54, "t1": 160.76, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3